<h2 class="ds-section-title">Use cases</h2>

<div class="ds-tabs" x-data="{ tab: 'replication' }">
  <div class="ds-tab-nav" role="tablist">
    <button
      role="tab"
      :class="{ active: tab === 'replication' }"
      @click="tab = 'replication'"
      :aria-selected="tab === 'replication'"
    >
      Replication
    </button>
    <button
      role="tab"
      :class="{ active: tab === 'migration' }"
      @click="tab = 'migration'"
      :aria-selected="tab === 'migration'"
    >
      Migration
    </button>
    <button
      role="tab"
      :class="{ active: tab === 'columns' }"
      @click="tab = 'columns'"
      :aria-selected="tab === 'columns'"
    >
      Column control
    </button>
    <button
      role="tab"
      :class="{ active: tab === 'cross-engine' }"
      @click="tab = 'cross-engine'"
      :aria-selected="tab === 'cross-engine'"
    >
      Cross engine
    </button>
  </div>

  <div class="ds-tab-body" x-show="tab === 'replication'">
    <div class="ds-tab-body-text">
      <p>
        Check that a replica, a restored backup, or a logical replication target holds the same rows as its source.
        Equal tables are answered by checksums alone, so nothing but a handful of hashes crosses the wire.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="ds-try-text">Try it yourself:</p>
    <div class="ds-terminal__command">
      <span class="ds-terminal__prompt">$</span> db-diff --source="$PRIMARY" --target="$REPLICA" --table=orders
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="ds-tab-body" x-show="tab === 'migration'">
    <div class="ds-tab-body-text">
      <p>
        Prove a migration moved the data and not just the schema. When a table does not match, DB Diff reads only the
        segments that differ and names the exact primary keys, so you get the keys that moved rather than a yes or no.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="ds-try-text">Try it yourself:</p>
    <div class="ds-terminal__command">
      <span class="ds-terminal__prompt">$</span> db-diff --source="$BEFORE" --target="$AFTER" --table=line_items
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="ds-tab-body" x-show="tab === 'columns'">
    <div class="ds-tab-body-text">
      <p>
        Timestamps and counters change on every write and will always differ. Include the columns that carry meaning and
        exclude the ones that only carry noise, and the comparison stays about the data you care about.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="ds-try-text">Try it yourself:</p>
    <div class="ds-terminal__command">
      <span class="ds-terminal__prompt">$</span> db-diff --source="$SRC" --target="$DST" --table=line_items
      --exclude=quantity
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="ds-tab-body" x-show="tab === 'cross-engine'">
    <div class="ds-tab-body-text">
      <p>
        Comparing a table between two engines is the one thing the open source tool will not do, and it refuses rather
        than misleads: a boolean is <code>true</code> in PostgreSQL and <code>1</code> in MySQL, so hashing each
        engine's own spelling would report every row as changed.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>DB Diff Pro</strong> reduces each value to a canonical form that both engines agree on before it is
        hashed, so the comparison means what it says.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="ds-terminal">
      <div class="ds-terminal__header">
        <span class="ds-terminal__dot ds-terminal__dot--red"></span>
        <span class="ds-terminal__dot ds-terminal__dot--yellow"></span>
        <span class="ds-terminal__dot ds-terminal__dot--green"></span>
        <span class="ds-terminal__title">refused by the CLI</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ds-terminal__body ds-terminal__gif">
        <video
          autoplay
          loop
          muted
          playsinline
          class="theme-light"
          aria-label="The CLI refusing a cross engine comparison (light theme)"
        >
          <source src="/assets/vhs/db-diff/cross-engine-light.mp4" type="video/mp4">
        </video>
        <video
          autoplay
          loop
          muted
          playsinline
          class="theme-dark"
          aria-label="The CLI refusing a cross engine comparison (dark theme)"
        >
          <source src="/assets/vhs/db-diff/cross-engine-dark.mp4" type="video/mp4">
        </video>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

